WEBVTT

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.900
There we go, nice and clean again.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.230
Why the extra effort? Did someone say they were stopping by?

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.730
Not really, but he still might come. Moriaki-sensei, that is.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.480
Oh? I thought you lost all hope and gave up.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.800
Today's love horoscope on TV predicted that this is the week

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.530
that you'll become more intimate with your fated someone.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.790
Channel Six did, anyway.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.250
Channel Six?

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.130
I flip through the channels and watch all the different ones.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.880
The last one I watched is my true fortune, though.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.520
Like the other day, the first one I saw predicted "poor luck".

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.760
So I tried other channels, but it just kept getting worse.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.600
Flipped to the last one, and it was the worst of all 13 signs!

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.240
13? I thought there were only 12.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.230
If it's in 13th place, I can't simply put my faith in "poor luck".

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.110
If I were 12th, it'd tell me,

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.470
"you're a persevering romantic Taurus."

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:14.990
But 13th place predicted, "Aries can get
things done, but can also be inconsiderate".

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.870
That fits you perfectly!

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.670
Goodness, I wish I could be as carefree as you are every day.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.610
Hee-hee, is it that obvious?

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.880
I bet my "intimate encounter" with my fated someone means Moriaki-sensei!

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:31.380
Couldn't your "fated someone" mean someone else?

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.350
Like your arch-nemesis, rival, or natural enemy, and stuff.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.200
Why would a love horoscope mention my natural enemy?

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.320
Hey, here comes your intimate encounter with Moriaki-sensei.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:44.730
Where!?

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.150
Extra lessons!?

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.030
Good for you, your fortune was accurate.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.560
Formulas.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:31.930
Formulas are equations that use variables to prove a certain value for a single set of data.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.730
Said values are referred to as solutions.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:45.750
Here, before my very eyes, sits my second natural enemy.

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:52.010
I recall my first natural enemy was my second grade homeroom teacher.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:59.880
When we read books, we all form our own unique opinions, right?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.560
The charm of literature is that there are as many answers as there are people who read.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.280
On the other hand, for math, there is only one correct answer for a problem.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.230
That's what makes math so interesting.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.870
I get it! I think I like math!

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:24.480
Uh-oh... we're not done yet, but we can't divide any further!

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.420
What do you think we should do here?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.920
She's right! What do we do?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.140
We can't do anything about the leftovers, so we write "remainder five" here.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:37.140
S-Sensei!

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.180
What's the matter, Moriaki-kun?

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:45.400
Umm, well, is it okay to just leave it unfinished like that?

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.230
You're right, it is kind of troubling.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.870
But there's nothing we can do about it.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.660
How would you handle it, Moriaki-kun?

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.020
I don't know...

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:02.130
But Sensei, you always say not to leave leftovers at lunch,

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.670
so is it okay to have leftovers in division?

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.670
He's right!

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.300
I agree with Moriaki-kun!

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.380
Thank goodness! I said that out of desperation, but everyone seems to agree with me!

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.180
That's true, it's bad to stop when there's still some left.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.670
But if you have a persimmon in your lunch, you leave the seeds, right?

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:26.190
The remainder in division is just like those seeds.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:30.200
Sit down already, Moriaki.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.530
Hehe stoopid! You eat persimmon seeds?

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.320
You're the stupid one here!

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:40.260
This experience would end up having a major effect on my life.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.490
This eventually led me to becoming a math teacher.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:51.990
My homeroom teacher became my first natural enemy.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:56.590
And now, in front of me sits the second.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:03.480
Umm, by any chance, am I the only one getting supplemental lessons?

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:11.900
The only person to get a zero on both the test <i>and</i>  the exam is you, Arashiyama Hotori.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.240
Oh, really? All right then...

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.100
Well, it's not so bad!

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.660
Just think of it as a date!

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:25.540
My stomach's beginning to turn earlier than I expected!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.750
Arashiyama Hotori.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.250
As a teacher, I hold good morals in the highest regard.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:36.220
Of course, I'm concerned about my students to a point,

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:42.350
but I'm sure you know how I would respond to that comment.

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.560
Yeah, I think I've got it.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:48.650
Very good. Now pay attention to me.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.440
When I was grading the tests...

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:58.070
Next one is... Arashiyama.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.060
It happens every time.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.470
As soon as I get to your test, my stomach begins to hurt.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:14.420
Despite the fact that you clearly gave up halfway, you still wrote the answer anyway.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.550
Naturally, the answer was completely wrong.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.330
Just the mere sight of it made me sick to my stomach.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:29.010
Before I could even consider the answer, seeing that bastardized square root gave me a splitting headache.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:30.970
And worst of all...

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.930
If you don't know the answer then just leave it blank!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:46.880
Just when I thought I had finally found a part of your test to circle,

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.680
it ended up being a zero in the score box instead.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:57.630
Grading your tests is without a doubt chipping away at my life.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:03.230
This is obviously the work of a serial exam murderer!

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.420
Oh my god!

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:10.010
You sure have a passion for melodrama.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:16.500
But to make matters worse, you're doing perfectly fine in all your other classes.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.430
I can only assume that you're doing this out of spite.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:24.190
But math's got nothing to do with being a detective.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.440
Detective?

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.370
Right now, I'm but an ordinary high school girl.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:32.860
But someday, I will become a genius high school detective!

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.630
Someday? How long do you plan on being in high school?

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.850
At any rate, if you keep this up, you won't move onto the next grade.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.680
So your dream might just come true.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.090
A 20-something year old high school detective is not outside the bounds of reason.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:53.810
And thus we're having these supplementary lessons.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.650
Now, solve this problem.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:58.630
Good...

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.180
Sensei!

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:01.930
Wow, that was fast.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:06.530
What's the meaning of this?

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:11.250
Do you know how to get that sphere into the house?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.840
Everything you need to solve it is already written here.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.280
Of course!

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:23.350
The sphere has a diameter of one meter from every angle.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:28.760
While the rectangular door's parallel sides make a constant one meter width.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:33.190
Thus, the sphere cannot pass through a door this narrow.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.130
It's impossible.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.980
The answer is simple.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:42.680
The sphere doesn't pass through the door.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.390
The house was built around it!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:51.730
This kind of outside the box thinking is critical in life.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:57.240
So for math too, if you give the answer first, it's easier to understand.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:05.120
I like corm.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.670
What gives Hotori? You're reading a textbook.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:14.220
That's a rare sight. Did hell freeze over or something?

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:19.170
Already has. At this rate, I'll be an eternal high schooler.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.470
Wow, I'm kinda jealous.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.080
Moriaki's furious at me!

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:26.550
Of course he'd be if you showed him a silly riddle like this.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:28.430
You know how he's overly serious.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:31.150
Just how serious he is, however,

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.730
can only be explained in a story I heard from an upperclassman.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:38.900
Years ago, there was a student in love with him.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.620
She was a pure, charming young girl with a passion for literature.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:44.960
That's just like me!

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.970
We're exactly alike!

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:47.500
Huh!?

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:52.440
One day, this girl poured her heart into a letter,

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.590
and handed it to Moriaki-sensei.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.920
The next day, she received his reply.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:01.410
What did it say? I wanna hear!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.400
Wait, don't, I'm scared!

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.430
My heart's all aflutter!

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:09.180
Only a single equation was written.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:17.420
Love between a teacher and student was not morally acceptable.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:24.510
And so she was ignored.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:27.370
The girl made such a fuss over it that it eventually reached the principal's ears.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.960
<i>Here's</i>  where your characters overlap.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.830
But the principal...

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:38.050
Moriaki-kun is a moral beacon in this age of illicit school conduct!

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.230
...was moved to tears instead.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:45.150
They say that it hangs in his office to this day.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.510
And they all lived happily ever after.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.600
What part of that is happy!?

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.490
You won't change his mind, so just let it go.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:55.940
If you don't buckle down and study, you really will be held back.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:00.960
They're alike.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:03.280
My two natural enemies almost overlap!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.780
Speaking in riddles completely unrelated to math and making me look like a fool.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.040
It's almost as if their faces resemble each other.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:18.140
Could it be that the adult Arashiyama Hotori went back in time to be my homeroom teacher?

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:20.530
No, don't be silly.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:23.420
I don't believe in that sci-fi hocus-pocus nonsense.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.140
I'm such a kidder...

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:31.010
Done!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.560
Lemme see. I'll check your answers.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:37.690
What the heck is this?

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:41.160
My answer to his equation.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.600
I'll show him this at the next extra lesson.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.010
You really are going to repeat this year.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:49.240
Formulas.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:54.620
The values of the variables within, are referred to as solutions.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:59.920
There are also cases when there is no correct answer.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.680
Here's your coffee, Moriaki-sensei.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:10.560
Thank you.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.640
And some for you, Kameda-sensei.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.100
'Preciate it. Pardon me.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.190
Way back, they used to say that

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:22.860
when you pour the milk in, it would float
to the surface and spell your soulmate's initials.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:26.610
I never took you for a romantic, Kameda-sensei.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.370
Never, huh...

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.620
If you squint your eyes, it kinda looks like it says N.M.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.210
As in Natsuhiko Moriaki, that is.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:38.140
Interesting. Mine looks like pi.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:40.210
He totally blew me off!

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.170
That's not even an initial.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.910
I suppose it means I'm fond of pi.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:47.320
Well, I wouldn't say I'm not.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.550
What about you, Kameda-sensei?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:54.220
If I don't see God's initials in mine, then I'm in trouble.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.350
Curse.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:04.400
What happened? It just collapsed all of a sudden.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:09.210
The height lever must be out of whack.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:13.130
I'm stumped. It falls every time I put some weight on it.

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:17.820
The desk next to me is open. How about you switch chairs?

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.170
I think I'll do that.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.490
This is a bad omen, I think.

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:23.550
The work of that "curse" initial maybe?

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:28.800
Don't say stuff like that, Nishi-sensei. It's not even an initial.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:35.930
Dear, come quick! Hotori's putting some weird goop on her face!

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:39.520
She said she's just putting on lotion so the air doesn't dry out her face.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:44.230
Our little girl's growing up, huh?

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:49.240
I wonder. She can't tell the difference
between lipstick and a glue stick, so I'm not so sure.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.660
What? What happened!?

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:56.620
My eyes! My eyes!

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.620
My face burns, and it stings really bad!

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.710
Yeah, the bottles look similar, so you must have mistaken it.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.340
Dad, you jerk!

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:10.650
Why are you using hair tonic when you aren't even bald!?

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:13.470
Idiot! It's thanks to that stuff that I still have hair!

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:17.970
It's hurting my eyes! I can't open them, so I'm going to skip school today.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.790
Don't be an idiot!

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:24.370
...and that's why I was late today.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:30.290
You've got some imagination. Your excuses never cease to amaze me.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:33.620
Well, they say truth is stranger than fiction.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:41.290
Grown up men sure have it tough, having to put that burny stingy stuff on every day.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.440
How's your hair holding out, Sensei?

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.190
Still there, no thanks to you.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:50.630
If I start losing hair because of stress, it'll be your responsibility.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:51.630
A shotgun wedding!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.970
You sure aren't the type who thinks before they speak.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:58.670
I'm going to begin class, so have a seat.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:02.040
We'll continue this later. See me after class!

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:07.230
Well, those kinds of things do happen.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:11.190
I brushed my teeth with face soap before.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.070
You're such a klutz!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.130
You're the last person I wanna hear that from!

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.600
Sure stepped on a landmine there.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.640
I told my story right after yours, so what's with the attitude?

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:26.110
I mean, normally after that nasty
taste, you'd be sure not to do it again.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.730
It's not like you've never done that yourself.

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.620
Hey, what the hell!?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:36.300
Called out for tardiness? What are you, a middle-schooler?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.060
So he was serious about staying after class.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.670
Well, Moriaki's a stickler for rules, you know.

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:44.680
As for how extreme he is, there's this story-

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.620
I know. The love letter.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:48.480
Tattsun told me about it before.

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:52.690
Love between a teacher and
student was not morally acceptable.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.270
Well, the story doesn't end there.

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:55.820
There's more?

00:16:56.030 --> 00:17:02.680
Five or six years passed, and believe it or not, she began working here as a teacher!

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:06.720
But there's still no sign that the feeling is mutual.

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:11.710
It's important to know when to give up.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.220
My, what lovely weather!

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:20.930
Better get home before dark, yes indeed.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:30.850
I tried to act natural and sneak by, but you caught me!

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:34.860
That was so unnatural that I
remembered the notice I wrote for you.

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:40.120
I got work soon, so make it quick.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.790
That depends on your behavior.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:47.560
I just had thoughts unbecoming of a teacher!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:52.460
Thoughts of sweet revenge for the daily torture Arashiyama puts me through!

00:17:57.170 --> 00:18:01.350
If I made her sit on that broken chair, she'd be in for a surprise.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:04.180
Such genius!

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:07.170
I never knew I had such a sharp sense of humor!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.260
What happened, Nishi-sensei?

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:21.780
Sorry, I just spilled some coffee, but I just finished cleaning it up.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.450
Oh, I see.

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:29.080
I have no idea which one's the sinking chair!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.770
It's regrettable, but I'm afraid the
"Spook Arashiyama Plan" is on hold.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:35.770
Wait a minute!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.590
Which chair should I sit in?

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:41.100
Minor offense lecture style.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.510
Mid-level offense lecture style.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.270
Serious Infraction lecture style.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:49.170
How should I approach this?

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.940
Which chair should I sit in?

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.320
What if my chair collapses and goes <i>ka-thud</i> ?

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:02.530
My dignity will collapse along with it!

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.910
Which one's the busted chair?

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:13.630
I can't tell from just pushing on them.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.210
If I had known this would happen, I'd have marked it this morning!

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:21.610
Just skip the lecture today!

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:25.010
Are you just going to run from your responsibilities?

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.320
Okay. I'm going to sit now.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:30.640
Sure, go ahead.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.230
Damn, she's not getting the hint!

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:38.490
I just realized that pi looks kind of like death!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:39.740
How ominous!

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:44.900
Just relax! Things like that aren't real!

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:50.500
The only truth here is the 33.33% chance this is the busted chair!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.710
Wh-What are you doing?

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.130
N-Nothing at all.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:20:00.400
Okay, Arashiyama. I'm going to sit down, so you sit down too.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.220
Well, okay then.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.440
No hard feelings, okay?

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:26.800
You're acting strange, sir. Babbling about 33.33% and stuff.

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:27.950
W-Well, you see...

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:35.210
Basically, in the span of a month, you're late 33% of the time. Yes.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.130
It's not <i>that</i>  often!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.240
Twice a week at most.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:43.970
Arashiyama, math aside, you can't even do basic arithmetic?

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:47.960
Um, six school days each week...

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:51.510
...and I'm late two out of those six...

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:54.410
Agh! Weren't we talking about tardiness?

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:57.110
Why are you trying to turn this into math class?

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:02.030
My class is on the level of mere arithmetic...

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:07.860
No! I've avoided the collapsing chair, so I can't allow myself to collapse either!

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:11.100
For her sake too, I've got to let her have it!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.980
Be stern, like a proper teacher!

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:28.670
As of now, the chance of us teachers retaining our dignity are zero.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:58.350
Thank you very maid for coming!

00:23:00.530 --> 00:23:03.820
Spaghetti, not pasta.

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:09.620
Today's love horoscope for Taurus is...

00:23:10.210 --> 00:23:12.200
Watch out for romantic troubles.

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:13.900
Poor luck...

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:18.760
Today's horoscope for Taurus
predicts bad luck with your studies.

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:20.690
Don't doze off in the middle of your test, 'kay?

00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:22.160
Poor luck again.

00:23:24.780 --> 00:23:27.070
Here's today's 13 horoscopes!

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:31.500
Aries' luck with money is at its worst today!

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:33.530
No, no, this one's no good either.

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:36.100
...and that's why I'm late today.

00:23:39.090 --> 00:23:40.330
Turn it off!

00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:45.000
Hey Senpai, don't you think Tattsun's kinda weird?

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.310
Yeah, she is a bit, that's for sure.

00:23:47.310 --> 00:23:49.600
How should I put it, it's kind of weird.

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:52.500
It's weird since depending on the meaning, it's not actually weird.

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:55.290
It's just kind of weirdly weird
when you force it into a sentence.

00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:57.400
That's just weird.

00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:59.710
What's so weird about me?

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:02.300
You can't just tell me?

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:03.960
It's weird.

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:08.090
Next time: The Amazingly Strange Tatsuno Toshiko.

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:10.470
The world still turns when it feels like it.
